            <ArticleTitle>Resection of left anterior descending coronary artery aneurysm on a beating heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the case of a 65-year-old man with unstable angina due to a left anterior descending (LAD) coronary artery single aneurysm. On a beating heart, the aneurysm was partially resected and the left internal thoracic artery was grafted in situ as a patch to the LAD opening. The patient remains well and free of symptoms two years after the operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
